how_its_made:
First of all, Cryptopia use @Filecoin web3.storage to store all the posts and projects' information. After a post is created, the cid returned by web3.storage is stored in contract and an event is emitted. 

@The Graph Subgraph will collect the post or follow events, and frontend use graphql to query these data.

@Sismo helps Cryptopia to verify project owner. We created a group and only if the project owner fits the criteria, the project can be verified.

Cryptopia uses @Axelar and @Wormhole to send cross-chain messages to broadcast these projects are verified. so projects only need to be verified on one network.

Cryptopia is deployed on testnets of Scroll, Mantle, Arbitrum and Polygon
